From: Talha Can Havadar <havadartalha@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 15:00:00 +0200
Subject: tensile: fall back to generic-family code object when the arch-specific
 hsaco is not present

The existing add-tensile-generics-support patch lets rocBLAS pick a generic
top-level Tensile library (e.g. TensileLibrary_lazy_gfx11-generic.dat) on
hardware whose specific arch (e.g. gfx1152) has no tuned library shipped,
and it lets initializeLazyLoading find Kernels.so-000-gfx11-generic.hsaco.
But per-solution fallback kernels are still resolved through
Tensile/PlaceholderLibrary.hpp::getCodeObjectFileName(), which builds the
filename from the runtime Hardware::archName() - always the *device* arch
(gfx1152), never the *loaded code object* arch (gfx11-generic). The
resulting name (e.g. TensileLibrary_Type_SS_..._fallback_gfx1152.hsaco)
does not exist in the package and hipModuleGetFunction later fails with
hipErrorNotFound, surfacing as HIPBLAS_STATUS_INTERNAL_ERROR (=6) on
every Sgemm/Dgemm call.

Fix the load-time fallback in HipSolutionAdapter so that, when none of
the xnack variants of the arch-specific hsaco can be loaded, we also try
the generic-family variant of the same filename. The mapping covers all
six generic families exposed by AMDGPU LLVM (gfx9, gfx9-4, gfx10-1,
gfx10-3, gfx11, gfx12); anything else falls through unchanged, preserving
the existing behaviour on architectures that don't have a generic parent.
This makes a rocBLAS build that ships only generic ISA targets fully
usable on any hardware HIP maps to one of those generics at runtime,
without any HSA_OVERRIDE_GFX_VERSION workaround.

The same fallback is added to initializeLazyLoading for symmetry - the
existing generic-library-discovery patch already makes the primary
Kernels.so lookup succeed via the generic arch, but the defensive
fallback here means the code still does the right thing if someone
strips all native targets from the build in the future.

The map is deliberately duplicated from
rocblas_internal_get_generic_arch_name() in rocblas_auxiliary.cpp
rather than plumbed through: Tensile is upstream of rocBLAS, cannot
depend on rocBLAS internals, and the arch->generic mapping is stable
metadata that changes only when a new AMDGPU LLVM generic family is
introduced.

Bug: https://github.com/ROCm/rocm-libraries/issues/214
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-07-13
